  "story": "V1-54 #167 criterion 4: LLM feedback as a weighted fitness signal, dev-partition ablation",
  "design": "paired by engine seed; the arms differ only in the run file's llmFeedback key (absent vs weight in 0.3,0.95). Endpoint is accuracy on held-out inputs the evaluator never sees, scored after the run by feedback_ablation_task/score_heldout.py, because both arms can reach a perfect visible score either by recovering the rule or by memorising the six visible pairs and only the held-out set separates those.",
  "interval": "median of per-pair differences with a 4000-draw seeded percentile bootstrap (seed 7). 6 pairs, and a near-bimodal endpoint, so a small true effect is not resolvable here; the discordant-pair counts are reported beside the interval.",
